## Managed by Ansible (roles/k3s-server) — do not edit by hand.
##
## k3s server config. Key names verified 2026-08-17 against
## https://docs.k3s.io/installation/configuration — the config file takes the same
## keys as the CLI flags with the leading dashes stripped.

## Disable the bundled Traefik so we can install a version we pin ourselves.
## See ansible/inventory/group_vars/mgmt.yml for why (ingress-nginx is retired;
## Traefik chart {{ traefik_chart_version }} is pinned by the rancher role instead).
##
## servicelb is intentionally left enabled: on a single node with no cloud load
## balancer, klipper-lb is what gives the Traefik Service an external address.
disable:
{% for component in k3s_disable %}
  - {{ component }}
{% endfor %}

## TLS SANs for the k3s API server cert. The public IP is included so the fetched
## kubeconfig works from outside the node; the Rancher hostname is included because
## the sslip.io name resolves to this same node and may be used to reach it.
tls-san:
  - {{ hostvars[groups['mgmt'][0]].ansible_host }}
  - {{ rancher_hostname }}

## Single-node cluster: this node runs the control plane AND the workloads
## (Rancher, cert-manager, Traefik). No taint, so nothing needs a toleration.
